From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 11:38:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 30/44] minimize: watch for firefox profile folders created
 later

A Firefox profile base (~/.config/mozilla/firefox, ~/.mozilla/firefox,
~/snap/firefox/common/.mozilla/firefox) that did not exist when the
watch started was never watched, so a profile created later, e.g. on
the first start of snap Firefox, was only noticed after the subscription
restarted. Each missing base is now watched for through its nearest
existing ancestor: when the next folder on the way appears, the profile
folders are looked up again, one level deeper each time, until the base
itself is watched. A folder created between the look-up and the watch
also triggers a new look-up.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BLrpLk9FRLLBEsz36L16sW

